    "body": "## Purpose\r\n\r\nAddresses the DeepSeek V4, V3.2, and V4.1 part of #57827. When a tool call ends without closing its final DSML parameter tag, final conversion drops that parameter. An unfinished `string=\"false\"` value can also be dropped when it is not yet valid JSON.\r\n\r\nThis change preserves the trailing parameter in final conversion. During streaming, it defers invalid partial JSON until its type is stable, so later chunks cannot invalidate arguments already sent to the client.\r\n\r\nAdds regression tests for streaming and non-streaming calls with string, numeric, and invalid JSON values.\r\n\r\nTogether, this PR, #58349 (MiniMax M2), and #58418 (GLM-4.7 MoE) cover all three parser cases reported in #57827. The issue should be closed once all three PRs have merged. This PR is distinct from #57707, which fixes Qwen3, and #53739, which changes the shared streaming engine.\r\n\r\nAI assistance was used to develop this change.\r\n\r\n## Test Plan\r\n\r\nRun the DeepSeek parser suites:\r\n\r\n`VLLM_TARGET_DEVICE=cpu .venv/bin/python -m pytest --confcutdir=tests/parser/engine tests/parser/engine/test_deepseek_v4.py tests/parser/engine/test_deepseek_v32.py tests/parser/engine/test_deepseek_v41.py -q`\r\n\r\nRun the repository's pre-commit hooks on the four changed files.\r\n\r\n## Test Result\r\n\r\n- 148 DeepSeek parser tests passed. The run emitted 14 Torch JIT deprecation warnings.\r\n- All applicable pre-commit hooks passed when run directly on the staged files.\r\n- No model inference evaluation was run. This is deterministic post-generation parsing, covered by CPU-only parser tests.",
